e asset into a renamed class.\"},\n {\"id\":\"dalvik-mini-interpreter\",\"concept\":\"answer computed by simple dex bytecode (char arrays, xor/add loops, StringBuilder, switch-flattened control flow) (rows 35, 43, 45)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Tiny pure-python Dalvik evaluator over androguard instructions for ONE method: const*/move*/aget/aput/fill-array-data/new-array/arith-int(lit)/if-*/goto/packed-switch + intrinsics String.<init>([C), StringBuilder.append/toString, String.charAt/length/getBytes, Integer.parseInt, Base64.decode. Step budget 50k, unknown invokes -> abort. Run it on static String-returning methods and on the proof= builder; regex the results. Handles string-encryption helpers and control-flow flattening without a device.\"},\n {\"id\":\"permutation-transposition-family\",\"concept\":\"keyless/known-plaintext transposition codecs (row 36)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"When a puzzle `data` is 20 chars containing exactly one each of A,N,S,- but no index list: derive the permutation from the known prefix and the public shape -- stride/affine slot map (i*k+o mod n, D17's order was (3+7i) mod 20), rail-fence (2-5 rails), columnar with width 2-10, even/odd interleave, chunk-reverse. Each family has <= ~200 parameter choices fixed by where A,N,S,- sit; keep only outputs matching ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ and require a unique match (a decode, never a submit loop).\"},\n {\"id\":\"reflection-name-resolve\",\"concept\":\"Class.forName / getDeclaredField / getDeclaredMethod with encoded names (row 43)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"androguard: find invokes of Class.forName, getDeclaredField/Method, Field.get, Method.invoke; resolve their String args (const-string, or via dalvik-mini-interpreter for decoded names), map to the real class/field in the dex and return that field's static value. Natural next step after R8 renaming in a resilience arc.\"},\n {\"id\":\"proguard-mapping-restore\",\"concept\":\"restore original names: mapping.txt / kotlin Metadata / SourceFile (row 45)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"If a question asks 'what was class a / method b originally' or the APK ships assets/mapping.txt|*.map|seeds.txt: parse the ProGuard mapping format (`orig.Class -> a:` + indented `type orig -> b` members) and kotlin.Metadata d2 string arrays + dex SourceFile/debug_info names; expose renamed->original facts and look up hint strings (`follow b -> a`) by original name.\"},\n {\"id\":\"apk-signing-block-payload\",\"concept\":\"hidden data in the APK Signing Block id-value pairs (rows 59, 62)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Every fixture has an APK Signing Block. Pure python: locate EOCD -> central dir offset -> `APK Sig Block 42` magic, walk the uint64-length id-value pairs, skip 0x7109871a (v2), 0xf05368c0 (v3), 0x1b93ad61 (v3.1), 0x42726577 (padding), 0x6dff800d (source stamp); return the other values (channel ids like Walle 0x71777777) and regex/decode_any them. Cheap hiding spot no extractor reads yet.\"},\n {\"id\":\"zip-structure-anomaly-scan\",\"concept\":\"ZIP-level tricks: duplicate names, local vs central mismatch, data after EOCD, archive comment, extra fields (row 62)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Pure python walk of local file headers independently of the central directory: report entries present only locally, duplicate names (Android takes the first; zipfile the last), differing sizes/names between local and central records, bytes between entries or after EOCD, the archive comment and non-standard extra fields; feed each blob to raw_entry_scan/decode_any. Catches a decoy entry shadowing the real puzzle JSON.\"},\n {\"id\":\"integrity-derived-key\",\"concept\":\"key derived from the APK's own integrity data (rows 49, 33)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Anti-tamper themes often key decryption on the signing cert SHA-256/SHA-1, the dex header adler32/sha1 signature, an entry CRC32 or the package name hash. Pure python: compute those digests (cert from META-INF/*.RSA via asn1crypto/pyca if present, else raw DER sha256), derive xor/AES-128/256 keys (raw, hex, first 16 bytes), and try them over ciphertext blobs found by static-key-cipher-decode; keep only ANS- matches.\"},\n]\ngaps=[g for g in new if g[\"priority\"]==1]+[g for g in keep if g[\"priority\"]==1]+[g for g in new if g[\"priority\"]==2]+[g for g in keep if g[\"priority\"]==2]+[g for g in new if g[\"priority\"]==3]+[g for g in keep if g[\"priority\"]==3]\nbody=\"\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False)+(\",\" if k<len(gaps)-1 else \"\") for k,g in enumerate(gaps))\ns=s[:j0]+\"```json\\n[\\n\"+body+\"\\n]\\n\"+s[j1:]\npi=s.index(\"Already built (prebuild-state ok, dropped from the list):\",i); pe=s.index(\"\\n\\n\",pi)\ns=s[:pi]+\"Already built (prebuild-state ok, dropped from the list):\\n\"+\", \".join(built)+\".\"+s[pe:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 -c \"\ns=open('reference/coverage/mobile-android.md').read();import json;j0=s.index('\\`\\`\\`json');j1=s.index('\\`\\`\\`',j0+7);g=json.loads(s[j0+7:j1]);print(len(g),[x['id'] for x in g])\na=s.index('## Recognition cues');b=s.index('## Readiness gaps');print('cue lines',s[a:b].count(chr(10)))\"; sed -n '/^## Readiness gaps/,/^```json/p' reference/coverage/mobile-android.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":927,"cache_read_input_tokens":71270,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":927},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b45ed517-057f-488b-ab73-e2c3b947a8a6","uuid":"04542501-a134-4bd2-bc43-cf0ed334486c","timestamp":"2026-10-17T13:12:30.499Z","request_id":"req_011Cg7sCBF